DESCRIPTION:The 21st annual Plymouth Folk and Blues Festival will take pla
 ce on Labor Day Weekend\, Saturday\, September 5 and Sunday\, September 6
 \, 2026\, from 2:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. Stars from Vermont and international
 ly known musicians team up for a lively two-day festival of folk and blues
  music performed in the pure country air of historic Plymouth Notch\, birt
 hplace of the 30th U.S. President. This year’s line-up will feature Grac
 e Morrison\, Tom Pirozzoli\, and Joseph Parsons on Saturday\, as well as K
 eruBo\, Sister Speak\, and The Kennedys on Sunday. Concertgoers are encour
 aged to bring lawn chairs and a picnic for this outdoor event. All concert
 s are free\, and cash donations to support the artists are appreciated and
  go directly to the artists. Food donations of unexpired non-perishables f
 or the Vermont Food Bank will also be collected. Calvin Coolidge State His
 toric Site\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
